    "bodyDocument": {
      "textSnapshot": "Problem:\nFour parser and snapshot-handling bugs prevented the provider from reading its own encoded output and misidentified JavaScript anonymous default exports.\nCompact snapshot line-length limit: A bufio.Scanner with a 16 MiB token cap could not decode snapshots it had just written. The encoder emits a single SnapshotSummary line carrying one record per parse/size failure, and repositories with enough failures exceed 16 MiB, causing \"bufio.Scanner: token too long\" at read-back.\nJavaScript default export false positives and misattribution: An unanchored regex \\s* matched leading whitespace across newlines, so exports preceded by blank or comment-blanked lines had their symbol report the preceding line's text. The regex also had no concept of comments or template literals, emitting phantom file-named symbols for export-shaped text in documentation or codegen templates. A containment test for \"class\" in the matched prefix misattributed arrow functions with class-named parameters as classes instead.\nGraphQL fragment spread name truncation: A fragment spread like ...ViewerFields was read as the field iewerFields (starting at the second byte), because the loop's continue landed at position +1 instead of scanning the whole spread name.\nSearch handler lookup failure on selective indexing: On repositories above MaxIndexedFiles, selective snapshot building from preselected files alone could select a commands/\u003cverb\u003e.json table without parsing the handler file it names, preventing the provider from attaching the verb alias to the handler symbol.\nSolution:\nReplace the Scanner with a bounded custom line reader that accumulates arbitrarily long lines in segments, since line length is determined by the artifact (encoder output), not by a predefined constant. Switch the default-export regex to ^[ \\t]* (space and tab only, no newlines), apply comment/literal stripping before matching (already done for SQL patterns), and fix the kind detection to inspect only the matched alternative. Fix the fragment spread loop to skip the entire name. Add a registration-table bridge to the search preselection: when commands/*.json files are selected, index the handler files they name (up to 4 files, scanning 50K paths, matching applied identifiers only).",
      "etag": "W/\"2026-09-04T07:05:35.996454Z\""
    }
  }
}
"}}

