atching byte prefixes, correctly handling whitespace-reformatted valid summaries like [ \"m\" , {...}] that the prefix match would reject."}], "page_number": 1}, {"title": "JavaScript/TypeScript Default Export Parser Fixes", "summary": "Corrects three failure modes in anonymous default export detection: wrong kind classification, incorrect source ranges, and phantom symbols from comments/literals.", "sections": [{"files": ["internal/sem/parser.go", "internal/sem/parser_default_export_regression_test.go"], "title": "Kind Classification from Matched Alternative", "description": "Fixed classification logic to read kind from the regex submatch alternative rather than searching the entire prefix for 'class', preventing arrow functions with parameters starting with 'class' (e.g., 'classifier') from being misclassified as containers."}, {"files": ["internal/sem/parser.go", "internal/sem/parser_default_export_regression_test.go"], "title": "Expression-Bodied Arrow Range Fix", "description": "Expression-bodied arrows (export default value => value + 1) now correctly report their own range instead of adopting the end line and body hash of the next braced construct in the file. Implemented bounded body brace detection anchored on match end rather than unbounded forward scan."}, {"files": ["internal/sem/parser.go", "internal/sem/parser_default_export_regression_test.go"], "title": "TypeScript Return Annotation Handling", "description": "Added typeScriptAnnotatedBodyBrace to find the body brace after complete return type annotations, correctly handling object types ({ ok: boolean }), generic types (Promise<{...}>), union types, tuple types, and conditional types. Distinguishes type braces from body braces by checking if preceding context continues a type expression."}, {"files": ["internal/sem/parser.go", "internal/sem/parser_default_export_regression_test.go"], "title": "Comment and Literal Stripping", "description": "Default export regex now runs against stripCodeLiteralsAndComments output, preventing phantom symbols from export-shaped text in block comments, line comments, or template literals. Preserves byte offsets so signature and hashes are cut from real source."}], "page_number": 2}, {"title": "GraphQL Fragment Spread Name Truncation Fix", "summary": "Corrects a defect where GraphQL fragment spread names were truncated, producing symbols that name nothing in the document.", "sections": [{"files": ["internal/sem/types.go", "internal/sem/parser_default_export_regression_test.go"], "title": "Fragment Spread Skipping", "description": "graphqlRootSelectionFields now skips the complete spread name (...ViewerFields) rather than resuming at the second byte, which was emitting truncated field names like 'iewerFields'. Loop increment now lands exactly on the byte after the name, preserving comment and bracket detection."}], "page_number": 3}, {"title": "Command Registration Bridge Implementation", "summary": "Implements a targeted bridge that adds handler definition files when command tables are preselected, solving the problem where verb queries matched JSON tables but handlers were never indexed above MaxIndexedFiles.", "sections": [{"files": ["internal/sem/search.go", "internal/sem/search_registration_bridge_test.go"], "title": "Registration Handler File Bridge", "description": "bridgeRegistrationHandlerFiles scans for commands/*.json files with 'function' fields in the preselection and adds up to 8 handler definition files (or remaining MaxIndexedFiles budget). Only actual definitions (via topLevelFunctionNames) consume budget, not call sites or same-named methods. Bounded by parse limit (64 files) and scan limit (50k files)."}, {"files": ["internal/sem/search.go", "internal/sem/search_registration_bridge_test.go"], "title": "Declaration vs Call Site Discrimination", "description": "declaresAppliedIdentifier provides a cheap textual screen that admits declarations and rejects calls before parsing. Checks that line prefix reads as declaration tokens (return type, qualifiers, func/function/static) rather than operators, statement keywords, or terminated lines. Prevents call sites from consuming parse budget when widely-called handlers have many more callers than definitions."}, {"files": ["internal/sem/search.go", "internal/sem/search_registration_bridge_test.go"], "title": "Budget Discipline", "description": "Bridge respects explicit MaxIndexedFiles as an exact ceiling - operates only on unspent budget after preselection. Git-tree-grep path gets its own budget (doesn't share MaxIndexedFiles cap). Already-placed handlers don't consume slots. Handlers chased in deterministic sorted order."}], "page_number": 4}], "title": "Parser and Compact Snapshot Robustness Fixes", "summary": "This branch resolves critical issues in compact snapshot encoding/decoding and fixes multiple parser defects affecting JavaScript/TypeScript default exports, GraphQL fragment spreads, and command registration bridging."}}}

